{"author":{"id":"2f242a7e7f2592f8909954a77fabece74f6e8cc197182647ed3b15ea8e3878af"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790977286,"nonce":"EuGWPOccMMBQLamA9RMd0J05ms8=","title":"Window.title reads back empty on X11","message":"`window_title` returns winit's `Window::title()`, which winit 0.30 does not implement on X11: it always returns an empty string (winit documents title as unsupported on iOS, Android, X11, Wayland and Web, though its Wayland backend does keep the title). Under Xvfb with openbox, a window opened with title \"xwindow-desktop-a\" reads back \"\".\n\nReproduce: `XWINDOW_DESKTOP=1 cargo test -p xwindow-check --test desktop` under X11; the check \"windows report size, title and monitor\" reads the title of each window.\n\nThe backend could keep the title it last set (from the attributes and `setTitle`) on its `Open` record and return that where winit gives none, so every platform reads back what the program set.","files":null}]}